#!/usr/bin/env bash
cat <<'EOF'
TMUX AGENT COCKPIT CHEATSHEET

Agent state / Herdr-like routing
  agent-pane [--agent k] [--cwd d] <name> <cmd>   launch/register an agent pane
  agent-status-scan                 refresh pane status
  agent-status-summary              compact status line
  agent-dashboard                   full status + key help
  agent-jump blocked|error|working|idle|done
  agent-explain <name|pane>         why did this pane classify that way?

Agent-to-agent coordination (Herdr socket-API equivalents)
  agent-list [--json]               registry + statuses, machine-readable
  agent-read <name> [--lines N] [--source recent]   read another pane
  agent-send <name> <text>          type into a pane (no Enter)
  agent-send <name> --keys Enter    press keys (Enter, C-c, Escape...)
  agent-run <name> <command>        send command + Enter atomically
  agent-wait <name> --status done   block until status (or --match <regex>)

Persistence / isolation
  agent-resume [--dry-run]          relaunch dead agents after server restart
  agent-resume <name> --session-id <id>   native resume (claude --resume ...)
  agent-worktree create <branch> --window  isolated git worktree + window
  agent-worktree open|remove|list

Cockpit keys — one prefix, then a key (prefix a puts you in the agent table)
  prefix a d      dashboard popup
  prefix a m      command menu (jump/worktree/resume/split/kill)
  prefix a s      refresh scan
  prefix a t      choose session/window/pane tree
  prefix a b      jump to a blocked agent
  prefix a e      jump to an error (crashed) agent
  prefix a w      jump to a working agent
  prefix a i      jump to an idle agent
  prefix a f      jump to a finished (done) agent

Your own tmux keys are untouched — the cockpit does not rebind pane navigation,
splits, zoom, copy mode, or the status-bar layout. Whatever you already use for
those still works.

Notifications (set in the environment tmux server sees)
  AGENT_NOTIFY=tmux|system|off      toast channel (default tmux)
  AGENT_NOTIFY_SOUND=on|off         audio cue; blocked/error beep twice
EOF
